[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1323","id":5096155105,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABL8En4Q","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1323","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1323.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1323.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1323","number":1323,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: run onepipeline's PR checks as lint plus one test job per platform","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAdds independent `lint`, `test-linux`, `test-windows` and `test-macos` PR jobs with developer-runnable, Nx-affected recipes. Consolidates Windows’ test shards and the previous macOS lane, shares install builds, restores main-built Rust caches, and avoids redundant release-PR tests. Also fixes a test-harness teardown race that killed another test’s newly started child process.\n\n## Why\n\nLong pull-request checks delay every merge and occupy slots in the account-wide limit of 20 concurrent jobs. Consolidating checks and cutting repeated builds reduces that pressure without splitting suites across more runners or reducing coverage.\n\n## Additional info\n\n**Rollout and limits.** Existing required contexts remain available while branch protection migrates. This change **does not achieve 30-minute test jobs**: committed timeouts are 30 minutes for lint, 180 for Linux, 270 for Windows and 210 for macOS. The old Windows shards and macOS lane are replaced by the new jobs; compatibility contexts report their results. Other retained checks still overlap during migration. Branch-protection changes and retirement of the remaining old jobs are separate work.\n\nThe user approved main-only cache warming on 2026-10-17: one build-only job per OS restores its previous cache and saves what PR jobs restore; PR runs do not save Rust caches. The macOS warm job skips pushes whose commit message starts with `chore: release`, and its runs-per-change budget increases from two to three. Linux arm64 remains supported by release builds and packaging, with no PR arm64 job. The macOS PR job runs on Apple Silicon.\n\nThe shared release shortcut checks tree differences and GitHub’s passing-main records, allowing only release-plz version/changelog edits; uncertainty runs tests. Lint never consults it. Separately, `test-macos` skips same-repository `release-plz-*` branches at job level.\n\nLint includes visual capture and reproducibility checks through screencomp composite steps. Preview publishing and comments remain with `visual-docs.yml` during migration (`VISUAL_DOCS_PUBLISH=false` in lint). MSRV and pinned-wheel release-compatibility journeys run in Linux’s test job to keep lint within its timeout. The release sweep remains separate pending retirement of the old jobs.\n\nOther build cuts include a Windows ReFS Dev Drive and Defender exclusion, shared install target directories, restricting stop-verdict compilation to its own integration binary, and moving judged lint into its own Nx project so its workspace-wide inputs do not select every Rust tier. Workflow-shape and scratch-workspace tests cover job contracts, cache keys, affected selection, failure propagation and the release shortcut. No tests, live/e2e paths or coverage floor were removed or sampled.\n\n**Hosted evidence.** The latest recorded completed run in which all four new jobs passed is [41268921847](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41268921847), on `9f2c6382`; Windows ran all 1,665 e2e tests. These are all-project runs because the diff touches shared Nx inputs. No hosted run on final head `224711ab` completed during the recorded work. Each figure below belongs to the named earlier head, not the final tree.\n\n| Run / head | lint | test-linux | test-windows | test-macos |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [41278937410](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41278937410), `35e6272a` | 739 s, passed | 6,333 s, passed | In progress when `1ac8a785` was pushed | In progress when `1ac8a785` was pushed |\n| [41268921847](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41268921847), `9f2c6382` | 881 s, passed | 6,948 s, passed | 7,097 s, passed | 4,362 s, passed |\n| [41259782580](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41259782580), `802520d1` | 632 s, passed | 7,235 s, failed: pinned-wheel timeouts under load; passed alone | Failed: origin separator expectation | 6,899 s, passed |\n| [41231576543](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41231576543), `4a424e3b` | 1,700 s, passed | 5,796 s, passed | 8,242 s, passed | 7,160 s: tests passed, artifact upload failed with `ENOTFOUND`; [rerun](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41231576543/job/124660931620) passed in 7,276 s |\n| [41218412386](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41218412386), `19301bd2` | 1,817 s, cancelled | 6,974 s, passed | 9,242 s, failed | 7,807 s, passed |\n\n**Required-check failures and repairs.** On `9f2c6382`, the retained required `gate` failed on `github_create_retry` ([job](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41268921847/job/124737453719)); the same journey’s origin expectation failed on Windows in run 41259782580. Earlier branch fixes were `46200ec4`, `35e6272a` and `47776845`, with `e77ea096` making the path-only `shadow_task` helper compile on Windows. Main subsequently landed #1330 and #1333, fixing the engine defect behind the flake—shadow refreshes losing the board link—and the separator expectation. Merge `224711ab` takes main’s version of `tests/e2e/github_create_retry.rs`; the final branch no longer differs from main in that file or `src/writeback.rs`. On the merged tree, the `github_create_retry`, `harness` and `profiling` e2e modules and library `writeback` tests passed (120 tests), and clippy `--all-targets -D warnings` was clean.\n\nOn `35e6272a`, the retained required `gate` failed on `profiling::a_process_running_several_journeys_writes_no_record` ([job](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41278937410/job/124766938155)). The profiled child’s nested `cargo build` of the doubles failed in 0.06 s with no output and passed three reruns. Both `install` contexts failed because their proof jobs depend on `gate`. The same empty `did not build:` failure occurred on [main’s push run 40984499366](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40984499366); this branch does not change `profiling.rs` or its build helper.\n\nThe cause was `World` teardown: after the last world decremented an atomic count, it ended every descendant over several process-table walks. A world created concurrently could start a child inside that interval, which the teardown then killed. `1ac8a785` replaces the count with a mutex held through the last world’s teardown, so new worlds wait. The regression test, `harness::a_world_made_while_the_last_one_tears_down_keeps_its_child`, failed at round 3 with the hold removed. With the fix, the harness and profiling modules passed (63 tests), the two race tests passed 10 repeated runs, every e2e module holding several worlds passed (697 tests), and both harness self-tests passed in all nine crates that include the harness (18 tests). Clippy and fmt were clean. Judged lint over `35e6272a..1181880c` passed: 7 passed, 0 failed. These are recorded repair checks, not a final-head full-gate pass.\n\n**Performance evidence and remaining cost.** All recorded hosted runs were cold; main’s warm cache becomes available after merge. In [41252290527](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41252290527), visual capture spent 15m58s + 2m37s + 7m50s on three cold release builds. Concurrent lint checks took 863, 1,249 and 697 seconds across observed runs; capture did not finish alongside the 1,249-second run. Disabling LTO and using 256 codegen units at opt-level 0 for capture reduced its local cold build from 31m30s to approximately 6m42s, with byte-identical shots. Together with moving MSRV and pinned-wheel journeys, hosted lint fell from 1,686–1,817 seconds to 632–881 seconds.\n\nRecorded remaining costs include Linux’s instrumented e2e (2,265 s), npm suite (approximately 830 s), cold instrumented build (approximately 750 s), live smoke alone (446 s), human-items (287 s) and bootstrap (263 s); Windows e2e (4,938–5,565 s), cold builds (approximately 1,630 s) and bootstrap (572 s); macOS e2e (4,546 s), cold builds (approximately 1,660 s) and bootstrap (411 s). Judged lint took 315–390 seconds. The committed test timeouts provide at least 1.5× headroom over the slowest recorded completed runs.\n\nLocal evidence is from earlier revisions, not a passing final-head gate. On the shared WSL host (20 vCPUs, global sccache), `just gate 7cab46a8` at a one-project `src/` change took **3,536 seconds and failed** because the host lacked `/proc/self/io`. Nextest cancelled remaining e2e tests, making this a lower bound. Load averages were 6.77 / 15.00 / 25.44 initially and 7.75 / 8.73 / 16.35 finally. The local 1,800-second bound was replaced with measurement/reporting under recorded ruling `c-c28da806de6de503b6d8c5eb7353a872`; coverage was not cut.\n\nBootstrap took 291–346 seconds. On `7cab46a8`, the earlier `ci-lint` selection took 391 seconds initially, including a cold MSRV build and a release-compat timeout under load; with cargo warm it took 15 seconds Nx-cold and 7–8 seconds Nx-restored at both workload shapes. On `22053d05`, all-project versus one-project selection contained 35/31 lint tasks, 22/21 Linux tasks and 26/23 Windows/macOS tasks. These figures predate the final placement of MSRV and release-compat in Linux.\n\nRecorded diff-scoped judged lint on `9f2c6382`: **27 passed, 0 failed**, history `20261101T032210Z-f0371`. No final-head full-gate or final-head hosted success is claimed.","created_at":"2026-10-31T09:03:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T09:13:39Z","closed_at":"2026-11-01T09:13:37Z","merged_at":"2026-11-01T09:13:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"40729afc16331bfc7b9b854d335674bccbac4001","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1323/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1323/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1323/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/224711abefde932106c3a9b8e75ea6dcb69da338","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/948/onepipeline-ci-speedup","ref":"nick/948/onepipeline-ci-speedup","sha":"224711abefde932106c3a9b8e75ea6dcb69da338","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155