ents":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1322/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1322/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1322/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/9d5e8f81a2c45c18eae8d7e7fb67d7543012e9da"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":{"enabled_by":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"merge_method":"squash","commit_title":null,"commit_message":null},"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278","id":5057128906,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABLW2pyg","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1278","number":1278,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf: cut onepipeline's per-test cost in the e2e suite and library","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nReduce e2e setup and process costs with shared builds and fixtures, batched repository seeding, native cleanup, and faster debug startup. Unobserved attached launches exit without an unnecessary two-second drain; maintenance reports reliably reach close-out, and large-root discovery reads launch records concurrently while preserving validation and order.\n\nThe existing crate and suite layout, per-case CLI coverage, scale assertions, and coverage threshold remain intact. Cached host fixtures reject malformed metadata, including duplicate live-run names.\n\n## Why\n\nWindows e2e tests averaged 21 seconds each, making the suite take over two hours and leaving the slowest platform to determine how long every change waits. Making each test cheaper preserves coverage and frees shared job slots sooner.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe measured reductions do **not** bring any platform below 30 minutes. The manager approved the projected overruns; shorter budget windows and replacing per-case CLI calls with in-process calls remain outside this change.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Performance evidence and remaining costs</summary>\n\nThese measurements precede the merge of main at `f5146966` and the subsequent fixture-validation fix at `56259ab0`; they are not measurements of the final tree. Baseline is profile run F (`c49dda5e-20e7-45fe-b6e2-995cad542eec`, 1,912 records). The later full recording is on `117e7352`, run `728f1477-5b41-4dca-b63b-19bea2d95958`, with 1,924 tests: 1,922 passed, one failed on missing host I/O accounting, and one timed out during a cold test-double build. The timed-out adoption test passed independently twice; the comparison substitutes its instrumented record from `75000004-f558-45a6-b4e7-31b2cfec86e0`.\n\n| Host Linux cost category, test-seconds | Baseline | `3de157d4` | `117e7352` |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Spawn | 21,300.6 | 15,107.6 | 13,337.3 |\n| Git | 1,097.6 | 753.1 | 897.5 |\n| Build | 6,542.3 | 12.0 | 150.7 |\n| Fixture | 51.5 | 20.7 | 29.4 |\n| Wait | 6,308.4 | 5,757.0 | 6,062.2 |\n| Filesystem | 334.0 | 168.7 | 244.2 |\n| Unattributed | 980.8 | 2,195.8 | 2,173.3 |\n| **Total** | **36,615.1** | **24,014.9** | **22,894.5** |\n\nProgram starts fell from 11,531 to 8,573 for `onepipeline`, 9,216 to 7,225 for git, and 3,764 to 6 for Cargo. Node starts changed from 39 to 68 and `ps` from 2,561 to 2,595. The later recording had higher host load: median load1 58.6 versus 45.6 at `3de157d4`. Its build category includes a cold rebuild after changing dependency optimization.\n\nPaired runs provide separate evidence: 130 CLI-heavy tests all passed in every pass, falling from 510.0 to 300.0 test-seconds (128.0 to 75.4 seconds wall, about 41%). Schema-registry startup fell from 133–186 ms to 23–39 ms. Across 57 publication tests passing in both temporary checkouts, paired totals improved about 20%; four additional old-checkout failures came from inherited discovery configuration and passed in the new checkout.\n\nThe projections apply the profile's platform/category ratios, schedule the exclusive group first and ordinary tests across four Linux/Windows slots or three macOS slots, and use the spike's p90/median ratios. They apply equally to the commonest one-project PR and a lockfile PR; no skipped suites, sharding, or crate split is credited.\n\n| Platform | Projected e2e test-seconds | E2e wall | E2e p90 | Job p90 including other work | With carried proof work p90 | Unattributed sensitivity p90 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Linux | 8,687 | 2,686 s | 3,308 s | 3,762 s | 6,513 s | 6,810 s |\n| macOS | 11,357 | 4,316 s | 5,181 s | 6,537 s | 8,107 s | 8,657 s |\n| Windows | 38,467 | 11,527 s | 14,291 s | 15,775 s | 17,832 s | 19,299 s |\n\nOther job work is the spike's 369 seconds for Linux (a lower bound), 1,129 for macOS, and 1,197 for Windows. Platform-only tests use the costliest test in their module as donor. Carried proof work is conditional on its placement in the later CI jobs. Linux's exclusive host-sized tests explain why projected wall time did not fall with aggregate test-seconds.\n\nCost-centre disposition:\n\n- **Spawn:** optimized debug schema/regex dependencies and removed the unobserved attachment drain tail. Per-case CLI calls remain. Most remaining publication git calls belong to `onevcs`; one four-node readjust journey starts 4,034 git processes, so that work was drafted for the sibling library.\n- **Test-side git:** repository seeding uses batched plumbing. Remaining starts are distributed across real repository journeys.\n- **Build:** successful test-double builds are shared across test processes; failures remain retryable.\n- **Fixture:** host-sized fixtures are generated once and copied with live-process identities rebound and journals independent. Scale assertions retain their scale.\n- **Wait:** existing pacing floors remain; deliberate quiet, release-poll, lease and takeover windows were not shortened. The channel journey ends its live listener with a reply instead of relying on a one-second assertion window.\n- **Unattributed teardown:** cleanup calls the same stop API used by the CLI, with environment restoration; explicit stop journeys still drive the binary. Skipping settled-run cleanup and replacing the `ps` reaper remain follow-ups.\n- **Filesystem and slow scale tests:** no further coverage-preserving reduction was identified. Publication chains retain their transitive-restack assertions. Windows Dev Drive/Defender configuration remains a runner concern.\n\nThe full per-module comparison, platform ratios, projections, paired logs and raw recording are retained under `/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-79`: `final-profile-117e7352/`, `pacing-profile-117e7352/`, `final-record-117e7352.{log,load}`, `compare-117e7352.mjs`, `project-finished.py`, `finished-comparison.json`, `finished-projections.json`, `previous-3de157d4-comparison.json`, `ab-*.log`, `pair-*.log`, `checks/`, and `checks2/`. Baseline raw records are no longer present; their retained aggregates are the comparison source.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence provenance and current limitations</summary>\n\nThe [required llmlint failure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/41174365927/job/124458737760) identified a launch-record comment left above code that now only collects paths. `fc8317f5` moves that explanation onto the reader it describes. `56259ab0` also rejects duplicate live-run names in cached fixture manifests, answering a subsequent boundary-validation finding. The added refusal case failed with the validation removed and passed with it restored.\n\nOn the final tree at `56259ab0`, judged diff lint exited successfully: history `20261031T061330Z-385f7` reports 17 passed, zero failed, 18 skipped and four not relevant across 39 rules. The configured local harness-wrapper path was missing, so the command selected the installed `oneharness` executable through `LLMLINT_ONEHARNESS_BIN`; no lint configuration or wrapper file changed. Rust formatting and e2e Clippy checks passed. The npm crate-split replay test passed 25/25. The host-view module passed 11/12, including the fixture-validation regression.\n\nThe remaining host-view failure is `host_view::the_host_view_answers_a_host_sized_root_steady_cold_and_steady_again`. This WSL host has neither `/proc/self/io` nor `/proc/thread-self/io`, so its cold-read accounting reports zero bytes. The assertion predates the task base (`61194ef6`, #861) and remains unchanged. The required Linux CI check supplies its verdict; no local green gate is claimed.\n\nEarlier evidence remains explicitly historical:\n\n- Main at `e357c4f0` was merged through `f5146966`, resolving the inherited `crate-split-replay` failure. On that merged tree, the affected check run covered 17 projects; targets passed except the e2e target and four dependent targets that could not start. A separate e2e run passed 1,959/1,959 in 3,802.591 seconds with the host-incompatible test filtered out. That full run precedes the final fixture-validation change and was not repeated afterward.\n- On `117e7352`, the new attachment-exit regression and related modules passed 181/181; before the fix, the new assertion observed a 2,069 ms drain delay. The rest tier passed 1,317/1,317 after installing the pinned tool, and contract/note/codex-server/stop-verdict passed 38/38. Budgets and crate documentation passed.\n- Coverage measured **96.00% lines** on the earlier recording and other tiers, after removing stale coverage binaries. It was not remeasured after merging main. The final tree's coverage floor, budgets and dependent aggregate checks remain for CI.\n- `10ec7848` added the missing-fixture repair diagnostic and its refusal case, plus explanatory test suppressions. Its host-view module passed 11/12, with the same host-accounting failure; the changed unwatched journey passed. Format and relevant Clippy checks passed. Node format/lint/syntax checks passed; release tests passed 58/58, workflow tests 63/63, and llmlint-diff tests passed. The then-failing npm replay test was resolved by the merge.\n- Judged lint history `20261031T020305Z-34ba7` reported two findings, answered by `10ec7848`. History `20261031T021304Z-a3029` then reported 18 passed, zero failed, 18 skipped and three not relevant across 39 rules. These earlier results are superseded for the final diff by `20261031T061330Z-385f7` above; the required hosted llmlint check remains the merge verdict.\n\nSuppression explanations retained in the diff cover the test-only Cargo recorder in `crates/testfakes/Cargo.toml`, the maintenance journey's real linked-sibling fixture and test-project boundary, and the unwatched journey's deliberately malformed/restored launch records. The latter state cannot be produced by a normal verb; assertions still read the binary's output. No suppression was widened.\n\nFollow-ups were drafted for `onevcs` publication git volume, lazy validator compilation in `onemessagebus`, and teardown/reaper costs. Evidence can be rendered with `onepipeline transcript ci-time-budgets-wave1 onepipeline-test-cost-r4`; merged-tree logs are under `/home/whoop/ai-orchestrator/runs/ci-time-budgets-wave1/scratch/857418-86`.\n\nThe existing draft is [#1278](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278).\n\n</details>","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:21:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T08:28:17Z","closed_at":"2026-10-31T08:28:14Z","merged_at":"2026-10-31T08:28:14Z","merge_commit_sha":"da460300fa11006304d74ef5c6d0f5763eeb2603","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1278/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/56259ab0e06b3331d08cad31e6ab15567d9c9302","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/ci-time-budgets-wave1/onepipeline-test-cost-r3","ref":"nick/ci-time-budgets-wave1/onepipeline-test-cost-r3","sha":"56259ab0e06b3331d08cad31e6ab15567d9c9302","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1327438417,"node_id":"R_kgDOTx8aUQ","name":"onepipeline","full_name":"nickderobertis/onepipeline","private":false,"owner":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"htt