:"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1278"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1278"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1278/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1278/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/56259ab0e06b3331d08cad31e6ab15567d9c9302"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1320","id":5092789912,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABL43OmA","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1320","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1320.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1320.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1320","number":1320,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf: cut the onepipeline gate's work outside the e2e tier","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nSpeed up the non-e2e gate by reusing the debug build, compiling the stop-verdict release binary alongside other tasks, and running staged-artifact corruption checks four at a time with faster fixture compression. Preserve every existing test and assertion, with regression coverage for build reuse, scheduling, artifact consumption, and build failures.\n\n## Why\n\nBring pull-request test jobs toward the 30-minute goal and make local gates faster without cutting coverage. Linux’s non-e2e work alone previously took 49.5 minutes, so skipping unaffected e2e suites cannot meet that goal.\n\n## Additional info\n\nComparable-load host measurements show median pre-e2e gate time falling from 8,090 s to 4,580 s (43%). Total non-e2e time is 8,931.6 + P seconds before versus 5,421.6 + P seconds after, taking the unchanged post-e2e phase as P. Its duration remains unestablished: the host’s cold-read e2e failure prevented a completed post-e2e phase; partial-input timings were collected for both unchanged post-e2e targets.\n\nChanges avoid `src/`, `tests/e2e/`, Cargo manifests and lockfiles, and budget files, keeping this work separate from the upcoming crate and test split.","created_at":"2026-10-31T00:20:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T05:02:12Z","closed_at":"2026-10-31T05:02:09Z","merged_at":"2026-10-31T05:02:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"0173e62498831d2770113d0c9a98143d416e134d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repo