,"user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nFix the Windows journey’s test shim to disable command echo, matching npm’s real shim and preventing echoed commands from corrupting JSON output. Add Linux coverage comparing the stand-in with npm-generated Windows shims, and make all four host journeys check intact arguments and exit status, with a Windows fixture that also works on ARM hosts.\n\n## Why\n\nThis host and its consumers are moving to the npm-installed engine. Fixing the test-harness defect at its source lets the pull requests they need pass while protecting consumers’ reliance on intact JSON output.\n\n## Additional info\n\nAlso updates the locked `libz-sys` to 1.1.31 for RUSTSEC-2026-0418.","created_at":"2026-10-29T12:05:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T17:46:20Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T17:46:17Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T17:46:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"5b7444724512778ea3912aa4db63aa2302a4a67b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":