ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nFix the settled-observer e2e race by waiting for the observer’s launch record before reading its ID: the judge can publish its PID before that record exists. Add a deterministic regression that forces this ordering and verifies the judge still ends when the observer cannot be signalled, preserving existing assertions and timeouts. Complete the crate-split mapping with the store tests’ borrowed review inputs.\n\n## Why\n\nThis test runs in a required job on every pull request. Fixing its synchronization removes needless reruns and keeps intermittent failures from obscuring real regressions, without retrying or loosening the test.","created_at":"2026-10-29T02:15:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T07:48:52Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T07:48:49Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T07:48:49Z","merge_commit_sha":"6103583a9dbecf9b4c31dbdc6a054f8aef2a1743","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1283/commits","review_comments