s): make the live-judge note journey wait for the worker's presentation record","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nMake the live-judge note journey wait for the driver to finish recording presentations before asserting exactly one worker presentation. Add a regression that holds the presentation append after note commitment, exposing the premature read deterministically while preserving the exactly-once assertion.\n\n## Why\n\nThe required Mac proof job takes about two hours, so a flaky failure forces another costly run and delays engine changes. Fixing the timing race addresses the cause instead of relying on reruns to pass.","created_at":"2026-10-28T18:03:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T21:14:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-28T21:14:21Z","merged_at":"2026-10-28T21:14:21Z","merge_commit_sha":"f098545dbb98350a0aef84fc81c4bd8a2a59bf1d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/o