","pushed_at":"2026-11-01T09:36:05Z","git_url":"git://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline","homepage":null,"size":24249,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":2,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":252,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":2,"open_issues":252,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1262"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1262"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1262"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1262/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1262/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1262/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/144f9b83449bcaa96b83956fd2f921ba90144627"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/978","id":4897965415,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABI_EFZw","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/978","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/978.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/978.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/978","number":978,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"test: attribute onepipeline's e2e test time and model a crate split","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nRecord per-test e2e costs in Nx outputs and CI artifacts, with analysis tools for platform comparisons and historical crate-split replay. Document measured optimization proposals, add a fence-retry regression, and stabilize a Windows maintenance journey while keeping its assertions.\n\n## Why\n\nPull-request checks take one to two and a half hours, delaying changes and occupying shared job slots. These measurements identify which changes can move Linux, Windows, macOS and local gates toward 30 minutes while keeping coverage.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe [profile report](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/blob/bd8116136f2ca2ee6f99e6344353a34fa4ead2b4/docs/test-profile-report.md) contains the 30 costliest tests and 10 costliest modules per platform, category shares and ratios, proposed crate mapping, per-suite unaffected fractions, prototype build measurements, and module-level coverage trade-offs. It preserves revision-specific checks, induced regression failures and earlier measurements. The [previous report](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/blob/47aac36/docs/test-profile-report.md) and [original report revision](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/blob/f2b95662c8cb847cb623eacfa5630629cd1633ed/docs/test-profile-report.md) remain available.\n\nRecording separates process, git, fixture, binary-build, wait and filesystem costs without double-counting nested work. Windows artifacts have distinct shard names; each shard must be passed separately to the analysis script because it selects one nextest run per label.\n\n**The proposed crate split buys no meaningful saving.** Replaying 144 first-parent, non-release merges from September 15 through October 15, 2026 against nine proposed suites skips **4.5% of suite runs** (58/1,296) and **4.2% of test-seconds**, versus 2.1% under today's layout. The result holds with both earlier CI weights and the latest local profile. Earlier 142-PR figures are withdrawn: the exclusive October 15 cutoff omitted #942 and #922.\n\nThe uninstrumented Linux prototype at f6a526e increases whole-job compile CPU by **38%** and incremental rebuild CPU by **36–45%**, while leaving per-test work unchanged. Building one suite saves 18–30% of compile CPU, but 95% of the replayed PRs require every suite. These measurements do not establish Windows, macOS or coverage-instrumented build costs.\n\n**Coverage decisions remain proposals.** Building doubles once per run, scaling configurable waits while preserving their ratios, and sharing the host-sized fixture are coverage-preserving candidates. Shortening budget-measuring journeys or moving per-case assertions to library tests would lose coverage and require the manager's decision. This change applies no crate split or coverage reduction, leaves the coverage floor unchanged, and does not establish the 30-minute target.\n\n**The latest Linux profile is a snapshot at 7a017fa.** Run `c49dda5e` ran 1,912 instrumented e2e tests in 10,293.5 seconds under shared-host load 44–106: 1,905 passed initially, and six failures passed when rerun individually with the same binary and recorder at that commit. The report names those tests and uses their second-attempt records alongside the other 1,906 original records. The remaining `host_view` cold-read failure also occurs at base 049ba74: this WSL2 kernel lacks `/proc/*/io` accounting because `CONFIG_TASKSTATS` is unset. It passes in hosted `gate` runs and is tracked in [#930](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/930). The earlier page-cache explanation is withdrawn. The sole subsequent commit, bd811613, updates the report only; these timings remain specific to the measured host and load.\n\n**Hosted evidence predates the latest merges.** In [run 39138389849](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39138389849), at 4b94e43, `gate`, `Mac PR proofs` and Windows shard 2 passed. Windows shard 1 failed a continuation journey at the sibling plan store's path check; it passed all three same-build reruns. Its Windows records cover 844 e2e tests and are reported per shard with matched-test category ratios, rather than a combined whole-Windows ratio. No hosted run at 7a017fa is claimed.\n\nIn [earlier run 39098714538](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39098714538), at dd2e5d6, matched-test time against CI Linux was **1.31× on macOS** and **4.99× on Windows**; Windows git, filesystem and spawn costs were **21.6×**, **9.6×** and **5.5×**. Windows produced 1,112 records and reached 1,108 of 1,413 e2e tests before its 180-minute limit without a failing test. Every other required job passed. Main's runs 39080139044, 39023278916, 39012247843 and 39008698390 also timed out on Windows. Earlier comparisons and local snapshots remain separately labelled in the report.\n\n**The Windows maintenance race is corrected.** In [run 39129002719, job 117680287750](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39129002719/job/117680287750), `maintenance::a_sweep_over_identities_that_declare_nothing_journals_nothing` failed once and passed three same-build reruns. Its one-second pace allowed a third sweep to start during closeout. Seven main Windows/macOS job logs and 48 loaded Linux runs did not reproduce it without this change, so the journey now uses a three-second pace with every assertion kept. It passed on Windows in 13.6 seconds and on macOS in run 39138389849.\n\n**The fence regression retains evidence of an early retry.** [The macOS job in run 39118487503](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39118487503/job/117656325734), at f2b9566, rewrote a refused publication fence after 167 ms. The added regression deliberately wakes the driver inside the five-second retry window and failed before the fix at 125 ms. Main subsequently supplied the stricter fence-retry implementation now present, so the net diff retains the regression rather than a product-code fix. The report preserves the original 78 fence/publication and 58 continuation passes and later merge checks with their revisions.\n\n**The engine refresh leaves no engine diff against main.** Earlier refreshes changed the permitted engine releases; the merge at a834bb3 takes main's lockfile and npm manifests exactly, including oneagentgraph 0.9.0, onevcs 0.57.0 and onevcs-testing 0.19.22. `engines-current` passed there. The report records subsequent mapping validation, the 42 analysis-script tests passing at 7a017fa, and earlier Rust, workflow, formatting, clippy and judged-lint results with their exact revisions. Those historical checks are not presented as a new full gate or judged-lint pass on the final head.\n\n**One lockfile change against main: pulldown-cmark 0.13.4 → 0.13.5 (5698c51).** The previous publication's required `deny` check failed on RUSTSEC-2026-0414 (exponential event growth with `ENABLE_WIKILINKS`) in pulldown-cmark 0.13.4, which comes in through onetaskgraph-core and onetaskgraph-plugin-api. Main's lock carries the same 0.13.4, so the advisory isn't from this branch. `cargo update -p pulldown-cmark --precise 0.13.5` changes only that crate's version and checksum. At 5698c51, `cargo deny --log-level error check` reports `advisories ok, bans ok, licenses ok, sources ok`, `just deps-check` and `just engines-current` pass with the engines unchanged, and `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` builds. That commit touches nothing the profile, the analysis scripts or the tests being profiled read, so the profile's evidence stands as recorded.\n\n**5698c51 is committed on the session branch but not yet pushed.** Its publication is blocked by the onevcs boundary gate on a removal that merge commit a834bb3 brought in from main. That commit is already on the remote, and the manager has taken the block to the user.\n","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:35:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T14:52:18Z","closed_at":"2026-10-28T14:52:18Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"910d4b17970d39c3f9763b1539807880b5f65df3","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/978/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/978/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/978/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/bd8116136f2ca