ertis/onepipeline/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-08T05:18:50Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T09:13:42Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-01T09:36:05Z","git_url":"git://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline","homepage":null,"size":24249,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"Rust","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":2,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":252,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":2,"open_issues":252,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1234"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1234"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1234"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1234/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1234/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1234/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/7f135587b664db3b18bf52b27a76839ca9ed76bd"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1230","id":5028642453,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABK7r-lQ","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1230","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1230.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1230.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1230","number":1230,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf(driver): hold the combined driver's cost flat across journal sizes","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAdds a release-only journal workload that holds activity delay, reply latency, idle CPU, peak memory and liveness journal growth across synthesized 1–800 MB runs. Reduces checkpoint rebuild windows from 16 MiB to 2 MiB so adopting an older run stays within the 200 MB memory budget.\n\n## Why\n\nLong multi-repository runs previously became more expensive as their journals grew, until the driver cancelled its own work. Measuring the combined engine and holding its results as budgets protects responsiveness as runs accumulate history.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe combined engine starts from main at `5970561d`, including op-journal-scaling (#1200) and op-envelope-outcome, and links onemessagebus 0.9.4 with its queue claim and submit cost fix (#195). The withdrawn op-claim-unconfirmed change (#1099) is not required or included by this work.\n\nThe Linux workload uses the release-built driver, the linked real `oneagentgraph`, and doubled model turns. Each seeded run has a 23-node plan and a schema-13 checkpoint shaped from `tests/golden/checkpoint-v13.json`. Four dispatches each have one heartbeating worker emitting activity every second; 20 amends arrive through separate `onepipeline reply` processes, one every 15 seconds. A 60-second idle window follows, with two observer members heartbeating and a `complete-but-draft` node keeping the driver attached.\n\n`onepipeline-journal-workload:workload` is uncached, non-parallel, and reached by `just workload` in the release sweep, outside per-change test selection. It writes `target/budget-records/journal-workload.json`, then checks five budgets. Their commands only report figures from that recording; thresholds remain in `budgets.yaml`.\n\n**Measurement provenance.** Final figures below come from the recording at `2c13a721`, the branch's final engine and workload code, produced through `bash scripts/nx.sh run-many -t workload -p onepipeline-journal-workload`. All five budgets passed. The earlier schema-15 comparison at `858f0e71` adopted the build's own checkpoint and did not rebuild the fold. Historical figures come from `driver-journal-scaling-2026-10-19-spike-driver-profile-report`, comparing v0.75.0 with main at `a77106ce` (0.78.0 plus #1036). Repeated historical measurements are retained; ≥ denotes a lower bound where the spike's phase limit stopped measurement.\n\n| Measure | 1 MB | 20 MB | 80 MB | 160 MB | 800 MB |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Event delay p95 before, v0.75.0 / main (s) | 0.09 / 0.09 | 499, ≥694 / 537, 496 | ≥1,491, ≥1,487 / ≥1,505, ≥1,509 | ≥2,754 / ≥2,727 | ≥4,102 / ≥4,330 |\n| Event delay p95 after (ms) | 30 | 28 | 26 | 28 | 27 |\n| Event delay p95, earlier schema-15 (ms) | 45 | 27 | 26 | 30 | 32 |\n| Reply answer p95 before, v0.75.0 / main (s) | 0.50 / 0.43 | 203, 146 / 226, 185 | ≥1,495, ≥1,494 / ≥1,465, 1,194 | ≥1,572 / 1,250 | ≥3,985 / ≥3,435 |\n| Reply answer p95 after (ms) | 435 | 432 | 353 | 448 | 504 |\n| Reply answer p95, earlier schema-15 (ms) | 675 | 360 | 462 | 486 | 625 |\n| Idle CPU before, v0.75.0 / main (%) | 1.6 / 1.6 | 3.8 / 3.9 | 17.5 / 16.0 | 69.6 / 67.0 | 101 / 106 |\n| Idle CPU after (cores) | 0.0212 | 0.0168 | 0.0172 | 0.0167 | 0.0168 |\n| Idle CPU, earlier schema-15 (cores) | 0.0290 | 0.0247 | 0.0268 | 0.0355 | 0.0367 |\n| Peak RSS before, v0.75.0 / main (MB) | 112 / 101 | 612, 610 / 612, 614 | 1,631, 1,584 / 1,543, 2,672 | 5,645 / 7,059 | ≥10,901 / ≥10,845 |\n| Peak RSS after (decimal MB) | 105.8 | 121.2 | 124.6 | 125.6 | 134.2 |\n| Peak RSS, earlier schema-15 (converted from MiB to MB) | 109.2 | 117.4 | 119.3 | 116.2 | 140.7 |\n| Liveness bytes/member-hour before, generated journals | 102,821 | 103,039 | 103,682 | 103,111 | 103,054 |\n| Liveness bytes/member-hour after and earlier schema-15 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe largest per-size figures are **30 ms** against the 1,000 ms event-delay budget, **504 ms** against the 2,000 ms reply budget, **0.0212 cores** against 0.05 cores, **134.20544 MB** against 200 MB, and **0 bytes/member-hour** against zero. Historical idle CPU figures are observed shares, not lower bounds; the 800 MB historical event-delay, reply-latency and RSS figures are lower bounds.\n\n**Checkpoint rebuild tradeoff.** The sole engine change reduces `REBUILD_WINDOW` from 16 MiB to 2 MiB without changing on-disk shapes. An older checkpoint requires rebuilding the fold, and each window occupies more memory after parsing and merge-ordering. At `73408c4f`, with 16 MiB windows, peak RSS was 107.4 / 230.4 / 218.8 / 209.9 / 276.2 MB across the five sizes. With 2 MiB windows at `2c13a721`, it is 105.8 / 121.2 / 124.6 / 125.6 / 134.2 MB. At 800 MB, adoption to the first loop-stats flush counting a finished pass increased from 24.0 to 48.5 seconds.\n\nThe new compiled-binary checkpoint journey crosses several rebuild windows, compares the rebuilt state with a fold without a checkpoint, and asserts exact record coverage and the final byte boundary. An induced record-count error failed that assertion with 5522 against 5521; the mutation was reverted.\n\n**Final recording detail**, in size order 1 / 20 / 80 / 160 / 800 MB:\n\n- Event delay p50: 16 / 16 / 15 / 16 / 15 ms; max: 66 / 309 / 405 / 207 / 100 ms. Every marked worker activity block reached the journal.\n- Reply answer p50: 270 / 318 / 247 / 343 / 322 ms; max: 440 / 549 / 361 / 1,294 / 543 ms. All 20 replies at each size exited successfully.\n- Submission to outcome in the command-outcomes queue, p95: 398 / 420 / 331 / 419 / 434 ms.\n- Adoption to first loop-stats flush counting a finished pass: 1.3 / 1.8 / 3.3 / 8.0 / 48.5 seconds. The earlier schema-15 recording at `858f0e71`, timed by the poll noticing the first pass, reported 2.0 / 1.2 / 1.4 / 1.5 / 2.3 seconds.\n- Each size recorded 76 worker heartbeats in `liveness.json`, whose maximum size was 824 bytes, and zero liveness-kind journal bytes. Other appended bytes remain classified by kind; at 800 MB these were 1,136 `turn-activity` records / 933,456 bytes and 20 `edit-committed` records / 126,580 bytes.\n\n**Reconcile timing limitation.** The reported distribution is over flush-interval averages, not individual pass durations. The engine counts passes but does not time them: each observed interval between loop-stats flushes, less one 200 ms channel wait, is divided by its pass count. Exact per-pass timing remains a drafted follow-up.\n\n| Final recording at `2c13a721` | 1 MB | 20 MB | 80 MB | 160 MB | 800 MB |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Interval-average p50 (ms) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| Interval-average p95 (ms) | 8 | 17 | 4 | 12 | 15 |\n| Interval-average max (ms) | 126 | 180 | 1,048 | 1,024 | 188 |\n| Observed intervals | 1,044 | 993 | 943 | 933 | 1,083 |\n| Passes | 1,122 | 1,119 | 1,108 | 1,066 | 1,202 |\n\nThe earlier schema-15 recording at `858f0e71`, computed the same way, reported p95 16 / 0 / 19 / 18 / 32 ms and max 390 / 456 / 408 / 204 / 436 ms over 1,104 / 991 / 1,126 / 1,177 / 1,077 passes.\n\nThe spike reported longest passes and envelope-phase medians rather than a matching p50/p95/max distribution. Its figures, v0.75.0 / main, were:\n\n| Size | v0.75.0 | Main at `a77106ce` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 MB | Longest 2.7 s; median 0.09 s over 1,100 passes | Longest 0.78 s; median 0.05 s over 944 passes |\n| 20 MB | Longest 537 s and ≥659 s; medians 37.7 s and 37.1 s | Longest 572 s and 530 s; medians 35.3 s and 40.7 s |\n| 80 MB | Longest 120 s and ≥1,496 s; medians 120 s and 125 s | Longest 158 s and 1,252 s; no pass finished in the second run's envelope phase |\n| 160 MB | Longest ≥2,745 s; no envelope-phase pass finished | Longest ≥2,745 s; no envelope-phase pass finished |\n| 800 MB | Longest ≥1,669 s; no envelope-phase pass finished | Longest ≥3,043 s; no envelope-phase pass finished |\n\nAt 800 MB versus 1 MB, final event-delay p95 is 27 versus 30 ms, idle CPU is 0.0168 versus 0.0212 cores, and interval-average p95 is 15 versus 8 ms. These satisfy the specified cross-size allowances of +250 ms, +0.0125 cores and +50 ms respectively, subject to the timing limitation above.\n\n**Budget enforcement evidence.** Against the final recording, an uncommitted copy of `budgets.yaml` with the RSS threshold reduced to 100 MB produced `budget driver-peak-rss: actual 134.20544 megabytes, budget 100 megabytes, headroom -34.20544000000001 megabytes (-34.20544000000001%) — over` and exit status 1. The original threshold was restored.\n\n**Scoped lint exceptions.** The workload project joins the existing release-only exception in `llmlint.yml` because its `check` reaches formatting and lint without selecting the workload. The generator's schema exception preserves the historical format and uses adoption as its drift check; the measurement reader's exception covers private formats whose unexpected shapes fail the workload. The budget reporter's three exceptions cover its paired producer/reader, end-to-end workload execution and onebudgetspec-owned result validation. The checkpoint journey's fixture exception covers constructing an older checkpoint and a long journal that no CLI verb creates directly. The former checkpoint unit-test exemption was removed because the new journey crosses the smaller rebuild windows.\n\nAll journals are synthesized from seed 20261019. Only aggregate calibration statistics come from real journals; no real journal content is included.","created_at":"2026-10-27T04:37:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T11:05:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-27T11:05:22Z","merged_at":"2026-10-27T11:05:22Z","merge_commit_sha":"2aac937cfef830d3f70e8996f6ef70d0e2a0819a","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1230/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1230/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1230/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/2c13a7215fdafd3b9325c3b0b853f9e531349125","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/1043/op-measure-combined","ref":"nick/1043/op-measure-combined","sha":"2c13a7215fdafd3b9325c3b0b853f9e531349125","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.co