/api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"merge_method":"squash","commit_title":null,"commit_message":null},"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1214","id":5011099115,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABKq9N6w","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1214","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1214.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1214.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1214","number":1214,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(release)!: hold a fast local-direct node's landing until the release it adopted early","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAllow `consumes` on `local-direct` nodes under both `fast` and `published` adoption. Accepted work awaiting an early-adopted release is preserved unlanded on its origin as `complete-but-held`; when the awaited releases arrive, it resumes on the same branch, re-pins and lands through the normal merge checks. The hold survives restart and adoption, remains visible as owed work, and blocks dependents and run completion.\n\n## Why\n\nRepositories that commit directly to their base need to consume releases and start work early just as change-request repositories do. Holding finished work gives them that early start without landing temporary pins or failing publication after the dispatch has completed.\n\n## Additional info\n\nBreaking public vocabulary: readers must handle status `complete-but-held` and outcome `held-for-release`. Release-held settlements, including awaiting-release drafts, now carry optional structured `awaiting` data naming each producer and target.\n\n`status --json` moves its run-reading schema to **version 3**, adding a per-node `nodes` list with status, outcome, detail and optional awaited releases. This breaks readers that require the previous exact schema version; the published schemas and contract are updated accordingly.","created_at":"2026-10-26T02:26:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T06:15:30Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T06:15:27Z","merged_at":"2026-10-26T06:15:27Z","merge_commit_sha":"969e83880165875967fafac20a7bfdd1b0d663cf","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1214/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1214/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1214/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/df5cc39d28d94d8a80363bf667d0b72de6c96637