.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/7621dd3c23302c71a24f92e73f762fa5aa9af50d"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":{"enabled_by":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"merge_method":"squash","commit_title":null,"commit_message":null},"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1128","id":4989673750,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABKWhhFg","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1128","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1128.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1128.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1128","number":1128,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(stop): end every process a node dispatch started, including turns started during the stop","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nOn Unix, stopping a run now freezes and rediscovers its dispatch trees before terminating them, catching processes started during the stop while leaving other runs untouched. Stops report incomplete discovery instead of false success when the host cannot establish that discovery finished.\n\n## Why\n\nA provider turn that outlives its run keeps spending network and quota with nobody watching ([oneharness#1442](https://github.com/nickderobertis/oneharness/issues/1442)). ai-orchestrator caught this race under load; closing it removes a source of flaky stop checks when adopting Codex plugins off by default.\n\n## Additional info\n\n- Windows retains the existing race: it lists once before invoking `taskkill`, so a child started between those operations can survive. A follow-up using Job Objects or thread suspension was drafted.\n- Regression proof: `driver::a_stop_ends_a_process_its_dispatch_starts_after_the_stop_has_listed_the_tree` failed against original base `6a8c0ac7` because the late child remained running after stop exited successfully, and passed on final head `12c0cf5a`. The test also requires the neighboring run to complete. The isolated base checkout retained its original `src/`; only `crates/testfakes/src/bin/fake-claude.rs` and `tests/e2e/driver.rs` received the fixture from `e1fc34c4`, using `git diff 6a8c0ac7 e1fc34c4 -- crates/testfakes/src/bin/fake-claude.rs tests/e2e/driver.rs | git apply`. From that checkout, `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/onepipeline-base-proof-target cargo nextest run --locked -E 'binary(e2e) and test(=driver::a_stop_ends_a_process_its_dispatch_starts_after_the_stop_has_listed_the_tree)'` failed after 82.1 seconds with the surviving-child assertion. On the final tree, the same command without `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` passed in 2.1 seconds. Cleanup targeted only the fixture's recorded PID.\n- Earlier retained results were three regression failures against base `6a8c0ac7`'s `src/`, three passes on `6344d3e0`, and three neighboring-run isolation passes. At `6cec5d6e`, the stop/shutdown/observer/driver/sys selection passed 297 tests and the late-child/orphaned-member/scratch/busy-review selection passed 32; formatting, deterministic lint, static llmlint validation and diff-scoped judged lint also passed.\n- After merging main's fixes, final head `12c0cf5a` passed all 186 tests selected by `cargo nextest run --locked -E 'binary(e2e) and (test(/stop/) or test(/shutdown/) or test(/observer/) or test(/scratch::/) or test(/review_round::the_busy/))' --no-fail-fast`, plus all 51 selected by `cargo nextest run --locked --lib -E 'test(/sys::|shutdown::|driver::/)'`. `cargo fmt --check`, `just lint`, and `just lint-llm-diff origin/main` passed; judged lint reported zero failures against `8737b646`. The complete local gate was not run.\n- The Windows scratch error 32 at `tests/e2e/scratch.rs:1440` in [run 40037144419](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40037144419) was an append open refused while the detached driver held the journal with `FILE_SHARE_READ`. Main also failed at `5b5c5436` in [run 39990392854](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39990392854). The test did not stop a run, and this branch's production changes did not alter journal sharing. Merged main's [#1129](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1129) shares reads and writes. A branch helper that became incompatible with that fix was removed; that later incompatibility was established from code, not a CI failure. The final scratch test is identical to main's and passes locally; this does not establish a Windows pass.\n- The macOS discovery-test failure in [job 120775746532](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40053993905/job/120775746532) came from a 50 ms test deadline expiring before a settling case completed. Settling cases now allow 60 seconds; deadline-expiry cases retain the short deadline, and the production bound remains two seconds.\n- Historical busy-review Windows timeouts also occurred on main at `a379ab5f` ([40032481568](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40032481568)), `5af95f01` ([39952566517](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39952566517)), `5cb58e35` ([40042776169](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40042776169)), and `64abf6f1` ([40049926671](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/40049926671)). The final tree includes main's busy-review process reduction [#1133](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1133) and watch fix [#1134](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1134); the busy-review test passes locally.\n- Earlier onevcs 0.56.9 trials exceeded the then-15,000 git-process budget on both this branch (15,224) and the merge base with the same dependency update (15,094); a onevcs follow-up was drafted. The final lock carries onevcs 0.56.10 / onevcs-testing 0.19.20. This diff leaves main's budgets of 17,000 on Linux and 25,000 on macOS unchanged; the finished tree does not enforce the original 15,000 limit.\n\nPrior implementation des