icenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":2,"open_issues":252,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1115"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1115"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1115"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1115/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1115/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1115/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/d21bf1ad108a6787df93f42b56d252cf35654bca"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1099","id":4957108049,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx8aUc8AAAABJ3d3UQ","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1099","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1099.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pull/1099.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1099","number":1099,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(driver): never end a driver's own dispatches for a claim it could not read","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nRead claims independently of reconciliation. Late, failed or rate-limited reads leave running work alive while an unconfirmed claim blocks new dispatches and publications; confirmation resumes progress, and another driver’s claim ends displaced work. Expose claim state through atomic `claim.json`, status, compact watch lines and one planner surface per prolonged unconfirmed episode.\n\nExtend takeover fences to in-flight dispatches across hosts. Every dispatch must be recorded on the store’s fence before starting; a takeover waits for evidence that displaced work has stopped or been released, never treating an elapsed timer alone as proof. Drivers proven gone allow immediate resumption on recorded branches.\n\n## Why\n\nSlow or rate-limited claim reads cancelled all four live dispatches in a three-day run even though the project still named its driver. Preserve those hours of work through ordinary host slowness and store outages while preventing overlapping dispatches during takeover.\n\n## Additional info\n\n- **Store outages now hold new dispatches.** The earlier best-effort fence left work invisible to adopters on other hosts; admission now requires its fence write to land. Already-dispatched work can still settle, and a run with no remaining work can complete without the store. Fence writes retry independently and coalesce snapshots arriving during a write into the newest pending snapshot. Terminal fence release shares the existing bounded writeback closeout. The outage journeys now remove the store after their nodes have dispatched; they no longer imply that new dispatches can start through an outage.\n- **Takeover waits are visible and evidence-based.** An occupied or unreadable displaced-driver fence keeps the adopter waiting. Before the successor run exists, stderr and all-runs `status` explain the wait; there is no run on which to raise a planner surface. For a driver on another host known to be gone, an operator can release its fence by clearing the project’s `onepipeline.publishing` metadata. This adds no release command. The pre-existing simultaneous-launch case with no stored claim remains outside this amendment.\n- **Moved-directory expectation:** the public-id journey now expects a renamed run directory with a dead local driver PID to require no wait and no ownership lock under that directory, because the dead PID proves the driver cannot act. A live PID still requires claiming and waiting. Successors reserve the moved run’s recorded identity so they cannot mistake its claim for their own.\n- **Compatibility:** JSON `claim` is additive and optional, omitted when no claim is known or no driver is live. Runs without `claim.json` remain readable. The generated schema and complete-field assertions account for the field. Adding `RunReading.claim` nevertheless breaks downstream Rust struct literals; the manager ruling in `docs/contract-divergences.md` accepts that change for a release already carrying a breaking change. Entry 139 records the amendment to #965. Watch heartbeat and ending lines add only `CLAIM UNCONFIRMED <age>`, at most 26 columns, leaving the rest unchanged; status retains the reason, full detail and age against the lease.\n- **Recorded request cost:** the comparable-plan writeback figures include every fence request. Relative to the base, `initialize` rises 4 → 19 (+15), `set_project_metadata` 4 → 21 (+17), `get_project` 5 → 7 (+2), attempts and `end_command` 21 → 27 (+6 each), `metering` 64 → 66 (+2), `update_task` 33 → 34 (+1), `calls_total` 138 → 181 (+43), and `requests` / `graphql_points` 45 → 65 (+20 each). These increases come from fifteen fence writes, two fence clears and the separate projection attempts required by admission after fencing. The journey waits for fence writes before advancing or measuring; it filters out no requests and changes no production scheduling. The cache-comparison and targeted-projection journeys also account for asynchronous fence writes.\n- **Observer teardown follow-up:** the earlier investigation of the [macOS stop failure](https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline/actions/runs/39829183931/job/120000630808) at `74a34b6c` identified the survivor as a restarted `fake-claude outlive-the-graph` judge, which ignores SIGTERM. After `stop_observer` killed the first judge, the unchanged `ObserverWatch::restart` started another graph within approximately 53–66 ms. The journal recorded two observer graph runs and a `partly-signalled` stop about five seconds after the first settled. With the same 300 ms widening after `stop_observer`, that branch refused 3 of 6 attempts and merge-base `b66f2aea` refused 2 of 6; every refusal had the restarted judge as survivor. Before stop, the driver’s process tree contained no store, claim-read or fence process. Unwidened, that earlier branch passed 18 of 18 on Linux. This evidence identifies an existing stop/restart race, rather than a process started by the claim or fence work; observer teardown remains unchanged and the race was routed to a separate follow-up.\n- The earlier Windows `cross proof` shard 2 timeout in `review_round::the_busy_review_round_ends_answered_and_true_and_records_what_it_spent` was also reported on the op-live-add-images, engine-incremental-read, op-ci-flakes and op-withdrawn-tasks branches. Shard 1’s `note::a_queued_note_its_receiver_refuses_is_journalled_and_leaves_its_outcome_as_it_was` passed its three reported re-runs. These are historical observations, not verification of the final tree.","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:22:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T04:47:36Z","closed_at":"2026-10-23T04:47:36Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"022002f34f4c10aa85e49094e8129445411529a6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1099/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/1099/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/issues/1099/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline/statuses/5bb33de3b3f962c7010b6e2f57b7d5e2c26a1abf","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nick/1042/op-claim-unconfirmed","ref":"nick/1042/op-claim-unconfirmed","sha":"5bb33de3b3f962c7010b6e2f57b7d5e2c26a1abf","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/us